  "reason": "The top-performing family is clearly scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer aggregation, with config_012 (vit_l, weighted) at 0.725 and config_019 (resnet50, weighted) at 0.713 but the best F1 (0.6945). Config_050 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the only remaining untested configuration in this top family. The evidence suggests resnet50 captures complementary image features (best F1 so far) and concat fusion performed nearly identically to weighted with vit_l (0.721 vs 0.725), so combining resnet50's discriminative strength with concat fusion could push accuracy past 0.725. This is a targeted exploitation of the strongest evidence with minimal uncertainty. Expected cost: ~5.5–6.5 GPU hours (similar to config_019's 6.22 h since architecture is nearly identical, only fusion changes from weighted to concat), which is moderate and justified given it is the most likely candidate to set the final best accuracy."
